# RelayFlow Cursor Rules


# RelayFlow Backend Rules

- Tech Stack: Python 3.11+, FastAPI, Pydantic v2, SQLAlchemy 2.0 (Async mode with asyncpg), Celery 5.3+, Redis 7, PostgreSQL 16.
- Architecture: Strict layered architecture (api/, core/, db/, models/, schemas/, services/, workers/).
- ORM Constraint: Strictly use SQLAlchemy 2.0 async style (`select()`, `AsyncSession`, `DeclarativeBase`). Do NOT use legacy 1.4 Query syntax or synchronous engine.
- Schema Constraint: Strictly use Pydantic v2 (`model_dump()`, `@field_validator`). Do NOT use v1 syntax (`.dict()`, `@validator`).
- Resilience: HTTP outgoing calls must strictly use `httpx` with 5s timeout and exponential backoff retry.
- Type Safety: Full type annotations across all files.
- Language & Documentation: All code comments, docstrings, and documentation must be written in professional English.
- Docs sync: After shipping new code or infra, update local `docs/changelog.md` (gitignored), plus committed `docs/develop_plan.md` and `docs/architecture.md` when structure or status changes.